        "knowledge_point_id": "8995cd9c-994e-54e6-8213-f832e7dbf978",
        "knowledge_point": "Finding Distributions of Squared Random Variables: One-to-One Transformations",
        "problem": "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.25$ | $0.55$ | $0.2$ |\n\nLet $Y=5-{X}^{3}.$ The distribution of $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $y$ | $4$ | $5$ | $a$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $c$ | $b$ | $0.25$ |\n\nWhat is the value of $a+c?$",
        "worked_solution": "First, let's add a $Y=5-{X}^{3}$ row to our table:\n\n| $x$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $6$ | $5$ | $4$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.25$ | $0.55$ | $0.2$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distribution of $Y$ is as follows:\n\n| $y$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.2$ | $0.55$ | $0.25$ |\n\nTherefore, $a=6,$ $c=0.2,$ and $a+c=6.2.$",
