        "knowledge_point": "Determining Whether a Vector Lies on a Plane",
        "problem": "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc$, $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨1,2,3⟩$, $c=⟨3,8,-7⟩$, and  $u=⟨9,22,-5⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$",
        "worked_solution": "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 22 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s+3t=9 \\\\ 2s+8t=22 \\\\ 3s-7t=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 8 & 22 \\\\ 3 & -7 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -7 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -16 & -32\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+8{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s+3t=9 \\\\ 2t=4 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n2t=4\\,⟹\\,t=2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s+3t & =9 \\\\ s+3(2) & =9 \\\\ s & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=3,\\,t=2,$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=3b+2c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=3\\cdot 2=6.$",
        "answer_fields": [
